Route conflict check: `GET /{documentId}/releases` vs `GET /{documentId}/releases/{publishedVersion}` vs `GET /{documentId}/releases/current` — distinct patterns, Spring prefers literal "current" over variable. Good.

Note: `/api/documents/{documentId}/terms/status` already exists with similar literal-after-variable pattern (`/terms/{termVersion}` vs `/terms/status`) — precedent confirms it works.

Validation: WithdrawRequest with @NotBlank reason, @NotBlank requestId, @PositiveOrZero expectedReleaseRevision. 400 on violation — handled by existing handler.

